  "mn114:11.9": "",
  "mn114:11.10": "As the examples will show, this refers to a kind of rebirth that is not conducive to developing wholesome qualities. ",
  "mn114:11.11": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Apariniṭṭhitabhāvāya</i> (“not for the sake of the state of perfection”) is found only here. The commentary explains it in terms of individuals who are reborn in a painful state where they are unable to realize the accomplishment of liberation. ",
  "mn114:11.12": "The question is absent in the Mahāsaṅgīti edition, but present in the PTS and BJT editions. ",
  "mn114:11.13": "",
  "mn114:11.14": "",
  "mn114:11.15": "",
  "mn114:11.16": "",
